{"t":"say","text":"Here is a typical seven-speed bike, with one front chainring and seven rear sprockets."}
{"t":"assembly","id":"seven-speed-bike","title":"Seven-speed bicycle","systems":[{"id":"frame","label":"Frame and saddle","summary":"Two connected triangles carry the rider and keep the wheels aligned. The saddle transfers the rider's weight into the frame.","explode":[0,0.3,0],"color":"#d4bf98"},{"id":"wheels","label":"Wheels and tyres","summary":"Tensioned spokes connect the hubs to the rims. Pneumatic tyres provide grip and cushion bumps.","explode":[0,-0.25,0],"color":"#c6e3ef"},{"id":"steering","label":"Steering and fork","summary":"The handlebar turns the fork inside bearings in the head tube. The fork holds the front wheel.","explode":[0.35,0.12,0],"color":"#9fbf8a"},{"id":"drivetrain","label":"Seven-speed drivetrain","summary":"Pedals drive one front chainring and a chain running over one of seven rear sprockets. A cable-operated derailleur moves the chain between sprockets and maintains chain tension.","explode":[-0.2,0,0.3],"color":"#e9a066"},{"id":"brakes","label":"Brakes and controls","summary":"Hand levers pull cables that close rim-brake pads against the wheels. A separate shifter controls the rear derailleur.","explode":[0,0.1,-0.35],"color":"#cfa7c9"}]}
